title: '2026-11-13: Jeff''s bare M on ''health \ jbb''. The server drew the old title; his history cannot say whether his buffer still showed it.'
pid: 162cd3ea-3016-4454-8fda-aa76b879b563
body: |2-
  Mission: [[id:aaddcc37-f159-4b48-9110-567482db4ebb][Find from Jeff's history why a changed node stood in his diff view with nothing under it]].
  Timeline, UTC: 20:02:02, Jeff retitled node 2fac9260 (pers-p) from a link
  titled 'medical, recent <2026-11-04 Wed> mess' to a link titled 'health \ jbb'
  (later staged, not committed). 20:34:05, he opened the diff view (buffer
  cabeb6e4), just after the client reloaded four of Top's notes. 20:34:31 and
  20:34:44, he saved that buffer (no file written: marks at most). 20:35:34, he
  saved a view of 'health \ jbb', which made a node titled with the old link and
  rerendered the diff buffer as collateral. 20:36:03, he asked for the node's file
  path; 20:36:09, that skgrepo's git index changed; 20:38, he wrote his example.
  20:53, he closed the buffer.
  On a copy rolled back to 20:34, without his example note, the diff view numbers
  'doing' 1q and the node 4l under 'pressing, by topic' 4h, as his did, and draws
  the old title under it as 4m, '(oldText title)'. Replaying his collateral save,
  saves of the unchanged buffer, and a save with the old title deleted (it is drawn
  again under a new ID) never left it missing. The code agrees:
  'expected_change_viewnodes' in 'server/refresh/diff_view.rs' draws the old text
  under an editable occurrence of a node in C with a Text leaf, which this was.
  So the old title was in what the server sent. What Emacs showed, the history did
  not hold: no buffer was logged, and folds stay in Emacs until a save. A fold
  explains it: 'health \ jbb' with its old title folded under it looks like a leaf
  but for '...'. The logging built for it is the view snapshots.
  What was put to Jeff about it, as content of his report, three questions:
  [[id:87ab808d-3a20-44a5-ada3-cc75ea208114][Your server did draw the old title under 'health \ jbb'.]]
  If he answers that the old title was not folded, the client's redraw is where
  to look ('elisp/skg-redraw-delta.el', and 'skg-replace-buffer-with-new-content'
  in 'elisp/skg-request-save.el'), which is Cleo's.
